{
  "result": "I've been thinking about mornings lately \u2014 not the big, productive, change-your-life mornings, but the small ones.\n\nThe kind where the light comes in sideways through the blinds and makes stripes on the floor, and the kettle is just starting to hum, and for a minute the whole world hasn't decided what it wants to be yet.\n\nI love that minute. It's full of quiet potential. You haven't checked your phone, you haven't remembered all the things you have to do. You're just... here. Breathing. Warm mug in your hands.\n\nI think we underestimate those little in-between moments. We\u2019re always waiting for the big thing \u2014 the trip, the promotion, the weekend, the *someday* when everything finally clicks. But most of life isn\u2019t made of big things. It\u2019s made of toast crumbs and good songs on shuffle and laughing at a text from a friend and the smell of rain right before it starts.\n\nIf I could tell you one thing today, just as a friendly thought, it would be this: pay attention to something small today on purpose.\n\nReally taste your coffee. Notice how the sky looks at 6pm. Listen to someone like you actually have time. Let something be delightful without needing to photograph it or turn it into a lesson.\n\nThe world is loud and fast and often a lot. But wonder is still everywhere \u2014 just hiding in plain sight, waiting for someone unhurried enough to notice it.\n\nSo here's to noticing.",
